      "stageId": "theory",
      "stageType": "theory",
      "stageSchemaVersion": 1,
      "title": "Understand the language",
      "instructions": "Read the explanation, examples, common error, and recap.",
      "required": true,
      "payload": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Greetings open a conversation and goodbyes close it. Choose the expression for the time and relationship. Hello is neutral, while hi is more informal. Good morning, good afternoon, and good evening refer to the time of day. After a first introduction, Nice to meet you is a polite response. When you leave, goodbye is neutral and See you is friendly."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "title": "Pattern",
            "text": "Greeting + short response; goodbye + optional good wish"
          },
          {
            "type": "example",
            "english": "Hello! How are you?",
            "explanation": "This complete model prepares the learner to say: Hello! How are you?"
          },
          {
            "type": "example",
            "english": "Hi! I'm fine, thank you.",
            "explanation": "This complete model prepares the learner to say: Hi! I'm fine, thank you."
          },
          {
            "type": "example",
            "english": "Nice to meet you.",
            "explanation": "This complete model prepares the learner to say: Nice to meet you."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The practical goal is to greet someone, respond naturally, and end a short conversation politely. Use the pattern in a short exchange, notice the other speaker's words, and answer with one clear idea. The examples below prepare the same language used in listening, pronunciation practice, exercises, and the final conversation."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "title": "Common error",
            "text": "Do not use good night to greet someone. In en-US, good night normally closes an evening conversation or comes before sleep."
          },
          {
            "type": "bullet_list",
            "items": [
              "Choose the expression that fits the person and situation.",
              "Remember the core pattern: Greeting + short response; goodbye + optional good wish.",
              "Answer clearly, then invite the other person to continue."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
